    {
      "id": "102",
      "type": "writeup",
      "attributes": {
        "id": 102,
        "body_ja": null,
        "body": "<p><span data-gp-id='70'>ましょう</span> is one of the conjugations of the <span data-term='助動詞・じょどうし'>auxiliary verb</span> ます, and is a common (polite) way to suggest that something be done 'together' (when used with a verb). It is often translated as 'let's (A)', or 'shall we (A)?'. To use <span data-gp-id='70'>ましょう</span>, we will simply need to change ます to <span data-gp-id='70'>ましょう</span>, when conjugating the verb.</p>\r\n\r\n<ul class='writeup-examples--holder'>\r\n<li data-study-question='155098'>\r\n<li data-study-question='155099'></ul>\r\n\r\n<p>Despite regularly being translated as 'shall we (A)?', <span data-gp-id='70'>ましょう</span> does not specifically target another person, and can also be used as a declaration that (A) will be done/needs to be done. This use reflects the base meaning of <span data-gp-id='70'>ましょう</span>, which is the polite volitional form (deliberately/purposefully doing something).</p>\r\n\r\n<ul class='writeup-examples--holder'>\r\n<li data-study-question='155100'></ul>\r\n\r\n<p>In this example, the speaker is expressing to themselves that they 'will' do something, and are strongly resolved to make it happen (similar to 'I shall' in English).</p>"
      }
    },
